  "macroOverview": "A bifurcated week defined the close of June. US30 printed a fresh ATH of 52,655 as value rotation absorbed Micron's blockbuster Q3 beat while NAS100 shed 4.2% from its weekly peak as rate-compression fears overwhelmed earnings euphoria. PCE May came in at 4.1% YoY (highest since April 2023), confirming Warsh's hawkish-hold anchor; monthly prints (+0.4% MoM vs 0.5% consensus) triggered a gold dead-cat bounce from 3,963. Gold's daily close of 3,990 on June 24 formally broke the 4,031 cycle low before recovering to 4,096 on Friday. ECB Sintra Forum (June 29 -- July 1) is the dominant risk event for the coming week. US Non-Farm Payrolls for June (moved to Thursday July 2 due to observed July 4 holiday) rounds out the binary calendar.",
